   "headline": "Alphabet's cloud doubles, but AI spending pushes cash flow negative",
   "facts": [
    "see fact packet: company filings and cited reports, 28 Oct 2026"
   ],
   "sources": [
    "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001652044/000165204426000080/googexhibit991q32026.htm",
    "https://in.investing.com/news/stock-market-news/earnings-call-transcript-alphabet-q3-2026-profit-miss-sparks-10-afterhours-drop-93CH-5662008",
    "https://fortune.com/2026/10/28/alphabet-google-stock-drops-cloud-revenue-doubles-free-cash-flow-negative/"
   ],
   "paragraph": "Think of a company that suddenly builds a huge number of factories before knowing the orders will fill them. Alphabet spent $51.4 billion on property and equipment in the quarter, against $24.0 billion a year earlier, driven by AI. Meanwhile Google Cloud revenue rose 103% to $30.7 billion, so customers are buying. Yet operating cash flow of $42.3 billion minus that spending left free cash flow at negative $9.1 billion, meaning more cash went out than came in. Net income fell to $26.2 billion from $35.0 billion, partly from an $8.7 billion paper loss on equity securities. Will the spending earn its cost back? That is unknown, and shares fell about 10% after hours.",
   "edited": "none",
   "explainer": "sonnet"
  },
  {
   "id": "microsoft-q1",
   "headline": "Microsoft's Azure grows 48% as capital spending doubles",
   "facts": [
    "see fact packet: company filings and cited reports, 28 Oct 2026"
   ],
   "sources": [
    "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/investor/earnings/fy-2027-q1/press-release-webcast",
    "https://investinglive.com/stocks/microsoft-q1-beats-as-azure-grows-48-and-capex-lands-6bn-below-forecast/",
    "https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/live/stock-market-today-wednesday-october-28-dow-sp-500-nasdaq-fed-meeting-decision-big-tech-earnings-130508769.html"
   ],
   "paragraph": "Azure is Microsoft's rental service for computing power: a company pays to use Microsoft's servers instead of buying its own. Azure revenue grew 48% to $33.165 billion, inside total revenue of $92.3 billion, up 19%. Meanwhile Microsoft spent $39.4 billion on property and equipment, double the $19.4 billion a year earlier. Analysts had expected about $46 billion, so the figure came in roughly $6 billion lower. Why? The quarterly number alone cannot say whether it reflects delivery timing, construction or supply limits, and that remains unknown. Non-GAAP earnings per share of $4.89 leave out the effect of its OpenAI investment, and shares rose about 4% after hours.",
   "edited": "none",
   "explainer": "sonnet"
  },
  {
   "id": "oracle-2030",
   "headline": "Oracle promises $225 billion of revenue by fiscal 2030 and caps new funding",
   "facts": [
    "see fact packet: company filings and cited reports, 28 Oct 2026"
   ],
   "sources": [
    "https://www.stocktitan.net/news/ORCL/oracle-investor-day-2026-accelerating-value-josi685spepl.html",
    "https://www.cnbc.com/2026/10/28/oracle-forecast-growth-2030.html",
    "https://www.fool.com/coverage/stock-market-today/2026/10/28/stock-market-today-oct-28-oracle-surges-on-fiscal-2030-revenue-guidance-of-usd225-billion/"
   ],
   "paragraph": "A target is a promise about the future, not a result. Oracle said it aims for at least $225 billion of revenue in fiscal 2030, which implies growth above 35% a year from fiscal 2026, with a 40% or higher operating margin. It also expects capital spending to peak in fiscal 2027 to 2028 and free cash flow, the cash left after spending, to turn positive in the second half of fiscal 2028. The catch: new stock and debt raising is capped at $20 billion through May 2030. How does the AI data-centre build get paid for inside that cap? Unanswered. Shares closed up 10.73% at $144.54, though analysts already expected $224.2 billion.",
   "edited": "none",
   "explainer": "sonnet"
  }
